course: dictionary
lesson: 1703
title: Words for sounds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A churr is a low, long trilling or whirring sound. Writers choose words like this to help you hear a scene. Context helps you work out what churr means when you have never heard the word before.
explain: «The nightjar, which frightened Toad in the night wood, is a bird that hunts moths at dusk, makes a long churring sound like a little engine.» The words «like a little engine» are the clue. An engine hums and whirs, so churring must be a humming, whirring sound.
explain: Churr can be a verb or a noun. You can churr, as a grasshopper or a partridge does. The sound itself is also a churr. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does the sound still make sense?
fact: To churr means to make a low, long, trilling or whirring sound.
fact: A churr is that sound, so it can be a noun as well as a verb.
fact: The nightjar is a bird that hunts moths at dusk and churrs on summer evenings.
fact: Grasshoppers and some insects churr too.
fact: Writers use churr in country scenes, such as in The Wind in the Willows.
exercise: «The nightjar makes a long churring sound like a little engine.» What does churring mean? | A loud crash like falling rocks | A sweet smell of flowers | A quick, sharp bite | *A low, long trilling or whirring sound
exercise: Which of these can churr? | *A grasshopper | A rolling stone | A sleeping cat | A glass of milk
exercise: «The nightjar hunts moths at dusk.» What does dusk mean? | Midnight, when everyone is asleep | Midday, when the sun is highest | Early morning, before breakfast | *Evening, as the light fades
test: In «a long churring sound like a little engine», what is the sound compared to? | *A little engine | A wave on the beach | A loud shout | A bell ringing
test: Where is the nightjar's churr a famous summer sound? | On top of a tall mountain | *On the heaths of Britain | In the middle of a desert | Under the sea
exam: Which is the best meaning of a churr, as a noun? | *A low, trilling whirr | A shout | A splash | Silence
